击球手。他失了两分。何塞·拉米雷斯有两支安打，纳撒尼尔·洛贡献一分打点。", "第五局，哈尔平将一记95.9英里每小时的球击出385英尺。球飞入右中外野看台。这是他的第一个季后赛本垒打。", "克利夫兰的牛棚非常强大。四名投手在最后四局只让一名跑者上垒。凯德·史密斯在第八局三振扬迪·迪亚兹，并守住了第九局。", "坦帕湾被三振13次。朱尼尔·卡米内罗被三振四次。第四场比赛在周五，但天气预报有雨。"], "body": "Gavin Williams struck out nine batters in five innings for Cleveland. He gave up two runs. José Ramírez had two hits, and Nathaniel Lowe drove in a run.\n\nIn the fifth inning, Halpin hit a 95.9 mph pitch 385 feet. The ball went into the right-center stands. This was his first playoff home run.\n\nCleveland's bullpen was very strong. Four pitchers allowed only one runner in the last four innings. Cade Smith struck out Yandy Díaz in the eighth and closed the ninth.\n\nTampa Bay struck out 13 times. Junior Caminero struck out four times. Game 4 is on Friday, but rain is in the forecast.", "body_zh": "加文·威廉姆斯为克利夫兰投了五局，三振九名击球手。他失了两分。何塞·拉米雷斯有两支安打，纳撒尼尔·洛贡献一分打点。\n\n第五局，哈尔平将一记95.9英里每小时的球击出385英尺。球飞入右中外野看台。这是他的第一个季后赛本垒打。\n\n克利夫兰的牛棚非常强大。四名投手在最后四局只让一名跑者上垒。凯德·史密斯在第八局三振扬迪·迪亚兹，并守住了第九局。\n\n坦帕湾被三振13次。朱尼尔·卡米内罗被三振四次。第四场比赛在周五，但天气预报有雨。", "text": "Gavin Williams struck out nine batters in five innings for Cleveland. He gave up two runs. José Ramírez had two hits, and Nathaniel Lowe drove in a run. In the fifth inning, Halpin hit a 95.9 mph pitch 385 feet. The ball went into the right-center stands. This was his first playoff home run. Cleveland's bullpen was very strong. Four pitchers allowed only one runner in the last four innings. Cade Smith struck out Yandy Díaz in the eighth and closed the ninth. Tampa Bay struck out 13 times. Junior Caminero struck out four times. Game 4 is on Friday, but rain is in the forecast.", "vocab": [{"word": "home run", "pos": "noun", "zh": "本垒打", "note": "棒球中击球手将球击出后得分的一种方式", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "strike out", "pos": "verb", "zh": "三振出局", "note": "投手让击球手挥棒落空三次", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "inning", "pos": "noun", "zh": "局", "note": "棒球比赛的基本单位，共九局", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "bullpen", "pos": "noun", "zh": "牛棚（替补投手）", "note": "指球队的替补投手群", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "series", "pos": "noun", "zh": "系列赛", "note": "多场比赛决定胜负", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "playoff", "pos": "noun", "zh": "季后赛", "note": "常规赛后的淘汰赛阶段", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "forecast", "pos": "noun", "zh": "预报", "note": "常指天气预报", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "lead", "pos": "verb", "zh": "领先", "note": "在比赛中处于优势", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Petey Halpin’s two-run homer lifts Guardians past Rays for 2-1 ALCS lead", "summary_original": "Halpin’s first playoff homer puts Cleveland ahead\nWilliams strikes out nine as Guardians win 3-2\nCleveland bullpen retires 11 of final 12 Rays batters\nPetey Halpin hit a go-ahead two-run homer, Gavin Williams struck out nine over five innings and the Cleveland Guardians beat the Tampa Bay Rays 3-2 in Game 3 of the American League Championship Series on Thursday to take a 2-1 lead.\nGame 4 of the best-of-seven series is scheduled for Friday, though rain is forecast.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Petey Halpin’s two-run homer lifts Guardians past Rays for 2-1 ALCS lead\nHalpin’s first playoff homer puts Cleveland ahead\nWilliams strikes out nine as Guardians win 3-2\nCleveland bullpen retires 11 of final 12 Rays batters\nPetey Halpin hit a go-ahead two-run homer, Gavin Williams struck out nine over five innings and the\nCleveland Guardians\nbeat the Tampa Bay Rays 3-2 in Game 3 of the American League Championship Series on Thursday to take a 2-1 lead.\nGame 4 of the best-of-seven series is scheduled for Friday, though rain is forecast.\nJosé Ramírez had two hits and Nathaniel Lowe added an RBI for the Guardians, who have won five of their last six playoff games since falling 2-0 behind the Chicago White Sox in their AL Division Series.\nWilliams allowed two runs over five innings while walking one. He is 2-0 with a 2.16 ERA and 33 strikeouts over 16 and two-thirds innings innings in four postseason appearances this year, including three starts.\nCleveland retired 16 of the Rays’ final 17 batters. Daniel Espino, Erik Sabrowski, Hunter Gaddis and Cade Smith combined to allow just one baserunner over the final four innings.\nSmith stranded a runner at third in the eighth when he struck out Yandy Díaz after a 10-pitch at-bat, then retired the side in order in the ninth.\nTampa Bay went down in order in seven innings, with Junior Caminero striking out four times. Rays batters struck out 13 times in Game 3 after combining for 14 in the first two games of the series.\nLowe opened the scoring with an RBI double in the second that bounced off the right-field fence and past Victor Mesa Jr.\nChandler Simpson put the Rays ahead with a two-run triple in the fourth.\nPatrick Bailey led off the fifth with a chopper that pitcher Griffin Jax was unable to field cleanly. Halpin then connected on an elevated 95.9mph sinker on a 2-2 count, driving it 385ft into the right-center-field stands to give Cleveland a 3-2 lead.\nIt was Halpin’s first postseason home run and only the fifth of his two-year major league career. Jax had not allowed a homer since 9 September, a span of five appearances.\nWilliams did not allow a baserunner and struck out five the first time through the order.\nJax allowed three runs on five hits and two walks in four-plus innings.\nExplore more on these topics\nMLB\nCleveland Guardians\nTampa Bay Rays\nBaseball\nUS sports\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-15T23:47:20.173050", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Gavin", "s": 0.3, "e": 0.625, "sm": 300, "em": 625, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Williams", "s": 0.625, "e": 1.025, "sm": 625, "em": 1024, "cs": 6, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "struck", "s": 1.025, "e": 1.3, "sm": 1025, "em": 1299, "cs": 15, "ce": 21, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "out", "s": 1.3, "e": 1.525, "sm": 1300, "em": 1524, "cs": 22, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "nine", "s": 1.525, "e": 1.8, "sm": 1525, "em": 1799, "cs": 26, "ce": 30, "si